evidence:
showBookEnd() calls tracker.flush(). flush() closes the last page (pages+1, chars+pageChars) and then restarts it (`shownAt = now`). The panel then covers the page, and every way out closes that same page again:
- 서재로 / home goes through onPause → pause();
- 다음 권 읽기 goes through openBook → closeCurrentBook → flush;
- 처음부터 goes through goTo → onPageShown.
Each adds another page, the page's characters again, and every second the panel was up (≥ 2 s) as reading time. Closing the panel with BACK and pressing next again adds one more page per round. ReadingTrackerTest.flushClosesThePageAndKeepsCounting pins this: the flush reports pages=1, and the later pause reports pages=1 again for the same page. Every finished book therefore inflates 쪽 / 자 in the statistics and the cpm used for 남은 시간.

computeKey hashes VERSION, ALGO_VERSION, font identity, book file size and mtime, font scale, layout settings and parse options. It does not include TxtDocuments.PARSE_VERSION or any EPUB split version. Before A2, VERSION_CODE invalidated every count on any update, parser changes included. A future PARSE_VERSION bump (allowed once per release by rule 6) that changes section text but keeps the section count would leave the old complete or partial arrays under the same key:
- PageCounts.setKnown only checks the length;
- countAll skips known sections;
- so the totals stay wrong until the user changes a layout setting.
This release is safe only because LayoutKeys.VERSION also went 2 → 3. The A2 rule and rule 6 in ARCHITECTURE.md say nothing about the count key on a parse bump.
